        ecrm:P3_has_note               "A machine knit ivory silk night cap, knit flat and shaped, then machine sewn with an ivory silk tassel"@en , "An example of 19th century male knitwear.  The development of the rotary knitting machine and application of steam and then electric power to knitting machines increased dramatically the knitwear output in Britain from the 1840s onward.  Knitted fabrics were particulary popular for underwear."@en ;
